BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Jukebox Turns Ten: St. Johnsbury
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261112
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261113
DTSTAMP:20261112T185931Z
UID:e1967e6a978fea9ac9ef6bacef8000@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:It’s our tenth season of Jukebox\, and we’re playing the h
 its\, deep cuts\, and brand new songs! This series will feature wholly uni
 que programs at our three stops\, as the repertoire is chosen in real time
  from 16 possible selections. You’ll hear music from the old guard of he
 avy hitters like Beethoven and Bach\, brilliant modern composers such as J
 essie Montgomery and Caroline Shaw\, solos\, duos\, and pieces that spans 
 the myriad of different styles and genres you’ve come to expect from our
  Jukebox quartet. With the help of the audience\, the program will be deci
 ded by chance as eight pieces are picked from our “jukebox” to perform
 . Every night will be one of a kind – it’s a game where we don’t kno
 w exactly what’s coming! Don’t miss out as we celebrate ten years of t
 his fun\, eclectic\, and intimate concert series.\n\nSources: Vermont.com
 \, Vermont Public
LOCATION:Vermont Symphony Orchestra\, Burlington\, VT
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/jukebox-tu
 rns-ten-st-johnsbury-10-08-2026-13-21-49
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Kirby Community Potluck Plus: Lands\, Legacy & Forestry Planning E
 vent
DTSTART:20261112T173000
DTEND:20261112T200000
DTSTAMP:20261112T185931Z
UID:c192230dd162c2da2709d1f8b53c8e@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:This potluck and presentation event is for Kirby landowners an
 d neighboring landowners (Concord\, Burke\, St. Johnsbury\, Lyndonville\, 
 Victory). We will be joined by: Kerry O'Brien of the Vermont Land Trust\; 
 Tricia Bhatia of the Forest Family Carbon Program\; Clarke Atwell\, Attorn
 ey\; and Matthew Langlais\, County Forester\, for presentations on land\, 
 legacy\, and forestry. If you are a landowner who is concerned about what 
 will happen to your land or forest as you plan for the future\, these pres
 entations will provide some guidance. If there is interest\, we will hold 
 a follow-up event in the spring. The potluck begins at 5:30\, with present
 ations starting at 6:15.\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Kirby Town Hall\, 346 Town Hall Road (Kirby)
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/kirby-comm
 unity-potluck-plus-lands-legacy-forestry-planning-event-09-10-2026-12-15-3
 1
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Nov. 12 | Walk With Me: Live watch party and Alzheimer’s convers
 ation
DTSTART:20261112T190000
DTEND:20261112T210000
DTSTAMP:20261112T185931Z
UID:de8705300175c6c167b4198631c58a@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Join Vermont Public for a live watch party of "Walk With Me" b
 y writer\, director and producer Heidi Levitt\, as part of Vermont Public
 ’s Made Here film series. Filmed over four years in unflinching cinema v
 erite mixed with archival footage\, the story captures the slow unravellin
 g of life with early-onset Alzheimer's disease. Hollywood casting director
  Heidi Levitt turns the camera on her beloved husband Charlie\, an award-w
 inning designer\, and their family\, as they face a disease that changes e
 verything. It is a story of love and loyalty as we come to understand livi
 ng with Alzheimer's and the toll of caregiving. See a preview here: https:
 //www.youtube.com/watch?v=hF4ejWTLyvs Following the film\, Vermont Public'
 s Nina Keck will lead a conversation about aging and Alzheimer's with Laur
 a Morin\, MSN\, RN\, CCM | Transitional Care Manager\, Rutland | Community
  Health Administration . Tickets are free but seating is limited. Please R
 SVP here: https://events.humanitix.com/walk-with-me-watch-party Schedule 6
 :30 p.m. - doors open 7 p.m. - Film screening begins 8:30 p.m. - Post-scre
 ening conversation 9 p.m. - Event ends Cancellation Policy Please let us k
 now by emailing events@vermontpublic.org if you are not able to join us so
  that we may release your tickets to someone else. Directions and Parking 
 Grace Church is located at 8 Court Street Rutland\, VT 05701 and free park
 ing is available on site. Other questions? Email us at events@vermontpubli
 c.org .\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Grace Congregational UCC\, 8 Court Street
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/walk-with-
 me-watch-party-and-alzheimers-conversation-02-11-2026-10-22-01
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Snow Movie Night at Patagonia Burlington
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261112
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261113
DTSTAMP:20261112T185931Z
UID:4ba309d5aa8863f9fc9f64ddc6fdee@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Grab a seat for a screening of two of Patagonia’s latest sno
 w short films. Run of show Doors open at 7:00p Films start at 7:30p Commun
 ity partner and beneficiary: TBD! RAFFLE! Your ticket will get you a free 
 raffle ticket for our raffle prize kit: a Powslayer jacket\, pant\, and pa
 ck! All ticket proceeds will go directly to our community partner who will
  be on site for the event. Film Synopses Simple as a Turn For Nicholas Wol
 ken\, turning is more than snowboarding’s foundation. It’s the simples
 t expression of what riding is all about. From going pro to shaping snowbo
 ards made for turns\, he’s spent much of his life chasing the deep feeli
 ngs that come with carving on snow. Sure\, the act of turning might be sim
 ple. But when mind\, body and board collide in a perfect toe-side\, simple
  has never felt more supernatural. Les Moulin des Artistes Some people mak
 e a living from their craft. Others can’t live without it. In a 16th cen
 tury mill in the Chamonix valley\, Peter Steltzner and Anati Graetz run Le
  Moulin des Artistes\, a ski workshop\, art space and gathering place for 
 like-minded free spirits. Whether it’s in Peter’s handmade wooden skis
  or Anati’s paintings and music\, Le Moulin des Artistes shows us what h
 appens when you devote your life to creative expression: how it can bring 
 purpose\, build lasting community and even help overcome disaster. 5\n\nSo
 urces: Vermont.com\, Vermont Public
LOCATION:Patagonia Burlington\, Burlington\, VT
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/snow-movie
 -night-at-patagonia-burlington-01-11-2026-16-08-46
END:VEVENT
