BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Learn from the Lawyers: A Legal Webinar for Artists
DTSTART:20261113T113000
DTEND:20261113T130000
DTSTAMP:20261112T185931Z
UID:30b1b58798d53cc0ff08e7dc896591@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Whether you have to suffer for your art is a question best lef
 t to philosophers. How to reduce that suffering is a question for an attor
 ney. Join the Vermont Creative Network and experts from the Vermont Small 
 Business Law Center to learn how being legally prepared for pitfalls can r
 educe problems for you and your business when obstacles appear. This webin
 ar with experts from Vermont Law and Graduate School brings together tales
  from a local artist\, mixed with expertise on how their business activiti
 es could use legal planning and protections to grow and continue creative 
 activities. Learn about protecting your work through licensing contracts\,
  handling AI scraping\, limiting liability from the public in your workspa
 ce or when interacting with your art\, as well as choosing the right entit
 y structure for your business\, hiring help\, and commercial leases. Q&A t
 hroughout is encouraged. Presenters: - Jeannette Eicks\, Professor of Law
 \, The Colleges of Law\; Small Business Law Center Founder\, VLGS\; Affili
 ated Faculty\, Stanford Law School - Sage Kochavi\, Assistant Director\, V
 ermont Small Business Law Center\; Owner\, Sage Kochavi Design Accessibili
 ty: This event will be live captioned by White Coat Captioning. We strive 
 to host inclusive\, accessible events that enable all individuals to parti
 cipate. We invite you contact us with the specific accommodations you may 
 need to facilitate your participation in this workshop. We will make every
  effort to honor your requests when they are made by Oct. 30\, 2026. Reque
 sts and questions should be addressed to Michele Bailey\, Accessibility Co
 ordinator\, at mbailey@vermontartscouncil.org or 802.402.4614. Voice and r
 elay calls welcome. Online\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Vermont Public is independent\, community-supported media\, servi
 ng Vermont with trusted\, relevant and essential information. We share sto
 ries that bring people together\, from every corner of our region.\, © 20
 26 Vermont Public | 365 Troy Ave. Colchester\, VT 05446
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/learn-from
 -the-lawyers-a-legal-webinar-for-artists-08-10-2026-15-26-59
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Mental Health First Aid training at UCS
DTSTART:20261113T090000
DTEND:20261113T160000
DTSTAMP:20261112T185931Z
UID:7ff3e469f6dc6bf22433e3c4db27e7@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Join the more than 2.6 million First Aiders who have chosen to
  be the difference in their community. Learn how to support your friends\,
  family\, and neighbors. Adult Mental Health First Aid (MHFA) teaches you 
 how to identify\, understand\, and respond to signs of mental health and s
 ubstance use challenges among adults. You’ll build skills and confidence
  you need to reach out and provide initial support to those who are strugg
 ling. You’ll also learn how to help connect them to appropriate support.
  This training is open to the public and is currently offered at no cost\,
  however\, space is limited. For more information or to register\, contact
  MLindsey@ucsvt.org.\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:United Counseling Service\, 100 Ledge Hill Drive
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/mental-hea
 lth-first-aid-training-at-ucs-19-06-2026-19-09-37
END:VEVENT
